From 0da77832b0a9d5a84ed969712088a7820e8dbcd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:29:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign server detail/creation screens as a labeled info
 card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the cramped one-paragraph server text with a clean labeled
layout (status, location, plan, resources, hostname, IPv4/IPv6 each
on their own line), matching the requested "Name: value" style.

Location now shows a flag emoji next to the city, computed directly
from the zone id's country-code prefix (e.g. "us-nyc1" -> 🇺🇸 New
York) via Unicode regional indicators — works for any country UpCloud
adds a zone in, not just a hardcoded list. IPv4 and IPv6 are shown on
separate lines instead of comma-joined. The server-created message
also now explicitly shows the root username, and upcloud_create_server
sets it explicitly instead of relying on UpCloud's implicit default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NFMuHFMb7r1xEwqxGw4pZn
